  "note": "Inside the modelled box this band is the marshy shore strip of the South Division, which the terrain spec builds at +1.25 ft from Andreas's 'strip of land along the river shore that was still more marshy, where land and water mingled, covered with tall grass, reeds and rushes', plus the toe of the west and north banks. NOT MODELLED HERE: the documented Public-Square-to-State-Street slough, the single most important vegetation feature inside the platted grid, runs about 480 to 840 m EAST of this 640 m box and has no ground in this scene. The north-side slough of Wright 1834 is inside the box but is a 7 m watercourse whose margin falls inside the marsh buffer of z04. The West Division swales are 0.6 to 0.8 ft deep and stay above this band, so they read as wet prairie with sedge patches rather than as sedge meadow."
